+// capped at 16 MiB class (kMaxProbeBytes) — a larger request is invalid
+// (code 3), never partially probed.
+//
+// CONVENTION LAW: unlike mincore (whose generic-trampoline form returns
+// raw-positive kernel errors), the write-copyin campaign observed the
+// -1/errno wrapper convention — while THIS TU reaches the kernel through
+// the same generic variadic trampoline as SYS_mincore above, whose
+// evidence-backed form is raw-positive errors with errno untouched. The
+// classifier accepts BOTH conventions WITHOUT conflating them: the raw rc
